---
import:
  - stdlib/lang/python
  - stdlib/cli/common
description: A command-line tool in Python 3.12 with Typer.
---

***implementation reqs***

- :Implementation: uses Typer, with its pretty exceptions off, in the package `app/`.
  - `app/cli.py` holds the Typer app, with a callback for `--verbose`, `--debug` and `--version` that sets up logging, and one module per command in `app/commands/`.
  - The work lives in `app/core/`, and the tool's errors in `app/errors.py`, under one base class `ToolError`.
  - `[project.scripts]` names the tool, `<tool> = "app.cli:main"`, where `main()` runs the Typer app and turns a `ToolError` into its message and exit code.
  - `pyproject.toml` declares a build system - hatchling, with `[tool.hatch.build.targets.wheel]` `packages = ["app"]` - so `uv sync` installs the package and the `<tool>` command: without one, uv installs no `[project.scripts]` at all.
- :Implementation: sets up the standard `logging` module to write to standard error with the level `--verbose` or `--debug` gives.
- :UnitTests: run commands with Typer's `CliRunner`.
